to-denny-vrandecic-source : List Word
to-denny-vrandecic-source = lines-of (cons "# Denny Vrandečić"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Head of Special Projects, Structured Content, at the Wikimedia Foundation. Co-developer of Semantic MediaWiki and Wikidata, ontologist on Google's Knowledge Graph, and lead developer of Wikifunctions and Abstract Wikipedia."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Every piece of your work that hyperactivity builds on is yours, with full credit. Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work established"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Across twenty years you have made one argument, in four systems: knowledge is not a pile of documents. It is structure, and a document is one rendering of that structure."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Semantic MediaWiki** put typed annotations inside prose; a sentence could carry a fact a query elsewhere would find. Prose and data stopped being separate artifacts."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Wikidata** made that structure shared across every language edition. Its decisive choice is one the knowledge-graph field still underrates: an item holds statements, each with qualifiers, references and a rank, and it keeps conflicting statements side by side, each with its source. It records who claims what, on what evidence, and lets the reader see the plurality. Most of the field built graphs on one correct value per slot. You built one that holds standpoints."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Abstract Wikipedia** takes the argument to its end. An article is written once, as abstract content, and a renderer for each language turns it into text. The article in Yoruba and the article in German are two renderings of one object; neither is a translation."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Wikifunctions**, live since July 2023, makes functions themselves shared knowledge: each with an identifier, a type, several implementations, and testers that check them. When four Google Fellows judged the plan at substantial risk and advised an existing natural-language-generation pipeline, the Foundation, with you leading the project, held the line: existing pipelines cannot serve languages such as the Niger–Congo B family. That was the correct call. The claim beneath it, that a function is knowledge in the same sense a fact is, runs deeper than its reception."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up from it"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Annotations become references by identity.** A source annotation denotes a typed host expression whose context includes the exact declaration it annotates; the association is a dependent index, not a textual convention"
  (cons (cite s6-4-p3 "(§6.4).")
  (cons "A definition is stored with its dependency references"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8),")
  (cons "so text that cites a definition depends on that definition itself. This page is built that way: every link on it is such a reference."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Statements with references become warrants.** What an observation warrants about a conclusion is a construction over every history compatible with it"
  (cons (cite s1-p11 "(§1),")
  (cons "and refining the observation can only shrink that fiber, so a conclusion established on the coarser fiber stays established"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1).")
  (cons "Combining observations constrains a joint fiber, and no global knower is required"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p8 "(§10.4).")
  (cons "Wikidata's choice to keep who claims what, on what evidence, with conflicting statements side by side, is the representation this semantics calls for: two sources are two observations, and what their conflict leaves open is the fiber compatible with both."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Language as the record it carries.** Words, their uses and their histories transmit distinctions no present speaker originated alone, and language belongs inside the history under investigation, not in a dictionary fixed before it"
  (cons (cite s1-p17 "(§1).")
  (cons "The interpretations compatible with an utterance at a state form a family, and different participants can yield different families"
  (cons (cite s1-p21 "(§1).")
  (cons "That is the setting a renderer for every language works in."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Renderers become views with stated laws.** A view is an interpretation of state, and bidirectional view laws state what round trips preserve and what is lost"
  (cons (cite s10-p11 "(§10);")
  (cons "for total views these are the lens laws"
  (cons (cite s10-2-p5 "(10.5),")
  (cons "and lossy views get their corresponding weaker or differently typed laws"
  (cons (cite s10-2-p6 "(§10.2).")
  (cons "A renderer's relation to its content is a stated property, provable beside the renderer."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Testers become paths.** The paper keeps three relations apart: definitional equality, a constructed proof of equality, and indistinguishability under a chosen experiment"
  (cons (cite s3-2-p2 "(§3.2).")
  (cons "Function extensionality turns a pointwise proof that two implementations agree into a path between them"
  (cons (cite s3-2-p6 "(3.10),")
  (cons "and equality then acts on every construction that depends on them"
  (cons (cite s3-p9 "(§3).")
  (cons "The path does not assert equal running time; that is a separate observation"
  (cons (cite s3-2-p7 "(§3.2).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Identifiers become content addresses.** A name is a view or alias, and renaming does not rewrite the computation"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "Address identity, definitional equality and a relation between meanings are three statements, each recorded with its evidence"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it serves"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your goal, as you have stated it: everyone able to share in the sum of all knowledge, in their own language, with the functions that render it held in common. Semantic MediaWiki, Wikidata's statement model, the separation of abstract content from rendering, and functions as shared knowledge are yours, with full credit, in this graph and in everything rendered from it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Denny Vrandečić, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denny_Vrande%C4%8Di%C4%87"
  (cons "- Abstract Wikipedia, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_Wikipedia"
  (cons "- Wikifunctions, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikifunctions"
  (cons "- Architecture for a multilingual Wikipedia, https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.04733"
  (cons "- Abstract Wikipedia team, https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Abstract_Wikipedia_team"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
